ked for a way to strike part of Sherman’s divided pursuit."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Sherman spread his armies across a wide front",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L16",null,{"seconds":439,"label":"7:19"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Sherman spread his armies across a wide front"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Thomas followed the railroad, Hooker and Schofield crossed farther east, and McPherson crossed at Lay’s Ferry."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Wheeler delayed the pursuit",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L16",null,{"seconds":518,"label":"8:38"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Wheeler delayed the pursuit"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Confederate cavalry slowed Thomas and McPherson, while Hooker and Schofield delayed each other during their crossing."}]]}]]}],["$","div","U.S. troops occupied Rome",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L16",null,{"seconds":593,"label":"9:53"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"U.S. troops occupied Rome"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A XIV Corps division and cavalry moved down the right bank of the Oostanaula and entered Rome on May 18."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Johnston used two roads toward Cassville",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L16",null,{"seconds":702,"label":"11:42"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Johnston used two roads toward Cassville"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Polk and Hood marched directly from Adairsville; Hardee and the wagon train moved through Kingston and then east."}]]}]]}],["$","div","Sherman divided his pursuit",{"className":"moment","children":[["$","$L16",null,{"seconds":807,"label":"13:27"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Sherman divided his pursuit"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"McPherson and most of Thomas moved toward Kingston, while Hooker and Schofield took the direct Cassville road."}]]}]]}],["$","div","The Confederate army concentrated north of Cassville",{"class